---
/**
 * /trust/: the catalog, provenance and the public numbers (ported from Silo/landing/trust, P1-06).
 * Every number on this page is live and none is baked into the build, so an unchanged rebuild is
 * byte-identical (the release id is content-addressed). Catalog counts come from SiloAPI /stats
 * and /categories (Silo developer's rule: no fixed catalog counts), API traffic from the
 * same-origin /metrics.json the host's counts job writes, and release download counts from
 * GitHub's public API (owner's choice, 2026-10-18; disclosed in the privacy policy).
 */
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SILO_API, LINKS } from "../../lib/site";

const endpoints = [
  "GET /stats",
  "GET /categories",
  "GET /mods?q=&category=&sort=&limit=&offset=",
  "GET /mods/:id",
  "GET /mods/:id/manifest?version=",
  "POST /mods/lookup",
  "GET /facets",
  "GET /img/:id",
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Trust and the Silo catalog · Silo"
  description="How Silo's catalog works: one record per Farming Simulator 25 mod across ModHub and GitHub, published builds hashed so your copy can be checked, a public read API, and the public numbers."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">The Silo catalog</p>
      <h1>One record per mod. Two sources. Checked against the published build.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Silo brings ModHub and GitHub together into one record for each Farming Simulator 25 mod, with the latest version
        found across both, and hashes each build from its source. So an installed mod can be checked against the build
        its source published. That is what the <strong>Verified build</strong> badge means.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/browse/">Browse the catalog</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#download">Get Silo</a>
      </div>
      <dl class="tiles" data-live-stats data-api={SILO_API}>
        <div><dt>mods indexed</dt><dd data-stat="mods">…</dd></div>
        <div><dt>ModHub and GitHub listings</dt><dd data-stat="sources">…</dd></div>
        <div><dt>categories</dt><dd data-stat="categories">…</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="small">Live from the catalog when the page loads.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="why" aria-labelledby="why-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="why-h">Mods scatter. The truth gets fuzzy.</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        A mod lives on ModHub, and its author ships newer builds on GitHub. Which is the latest? Is the file you
        downloaded the one the author actually published, or was it repacked with something extra? The catalog answers
        both.
      </p>
      <div class="cols">
        <div>
          <h3>One record per mod</h3>
          <p>A mod's ModHub and GitHub listings resolve to one record, so you see the latest version found across both.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Provenance, not a virus scan</h3>
          <p>
            We hash published builds. Silo hashes your installed copy on your computer and compares: a clean match, or the
            exact files that differ. It confirms what a mod is. It doesn't guess intent.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>What's covered</h3>
          <p>
            An hourly job refreshes versions and metadata, most popular mods first. Silo can only check ModHub versions it hashed
            before ModHub fetching was paused. GitHub versions are checked as usual.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3 class="legend-h">What you'll see in Silo and on Browse</h3>
      <ul class="legend">
        <li><span class="badge ok">Verified build</span> Your copy matches the published build byte for byte.</li>
        <li><span class="badge warn">Modified (2 files)</span> Your copy differs from the published build; Silo lists the files.</li>
        <li><span class="badge none">No badge</span> The catalog has no published build on file to compare against.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hosting" aria-labelledby="hosting-h">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <h2 id="hosting-h">Silo indexes. It doesn't host.</h2>
      <p>
        Silo indexes public mod information and links back to each source. It does not host, mirror or redistribute mod
        files. Downloads always go to the original source, whose own terms apply.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our catalog server keeps cover images and integrity hashes it cached earlier, ModHub ones included. We keep those
        to show what the full platform can do, should GIANTS allow us an official feed. We've asked them. Until then, the
        server fetches nothing new from GIANTS' CDN, and we'll remove the ModHub cache if GIANTS asks us to.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="authors" aria-labelledby="authors-h">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="kicker">For mod authors</p>
      <h2 id="authors-h">Help us get your builds right.</h2>
      <p>
        Provenance is only as good as its source of truth, and no one knows a mod's real build better than the person who
        made it. We'd like mod authors to be able to confirm their own builds. There's no way to do that yet. When Silo has
        your published build on file, players can check whether their copy matches it.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your mod is listed wrongly, or you'd rather it wasn't listed, tell us and we'll fix it: open an issue on <a
          href={LINKS.newIssue}>GitHub</a
        > or email <a href="mailto:legal@hllmr.com">legal@hllmr.com</a>. See also <a href="/legal/copyright-takedown.html"
          >Copyright &amp; Takedown</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="api" aria-labelledby="api-h">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="kicker">For developers</p>
      <h2 id="api-h">A public read API.</h2>
      <p>
        The catalog is served by SiloAPI, a public, read-only HTTP API. No key, no account. It's rate-limited, so please be
        a good citizen. It aggregates public metadata and links back to sources.
      </p>
      <p>Base: <code>{SILO_API}</code></p>
      <ul class="endpoints">{endpoints.map((e) => <li><code>{e}</code></li>)}</ul>
      <p>The <a href="/browse/">Browse</a> page is built entirely on these endpoints.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="numbers" aria-labelledby="numbers-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">For nerds</p>
      <h2 id="numbers-h">The whole system, by the numbers.</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        Aggregate counts only. There's no account and no telemetry, and the app contacts the catalog only when you search
        Browse, open a mod's details, check for updates or verify a mod. Traffic numbers come from our server access logs,
        which keep IP addresses for 30 days (see the <a href="/legal/privacy-policy.html">privacy policy</a>). Small numbers
        are shown as they are.
      </p>

      <div class="grid2">
        <div class="panel" data-live-downloads data-repo-api="https://api.github.com/repos/HLLMR/silo/releases?per_page=100">
          <h3>Downloads by release</h3>
          <p class="big"><span data-dl-total>…</span> <span>installer and app-package downloads<span data-dl-releases></span></span></p>
          <table class="bars">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Release</th>
                <th scope="col">Downloads</th>
                <th scope="col" class="bar-col"><span class="visually-hidden">Share</span></th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody data-dl-rows></tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="small" data-dl-note>
            Installer and app-package files only (.exe, .msi, .dmg, .AppImage, .deb, .rpm), read from GitHub's public release
            data when the page loads.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="panel" data-live-metrics>
          <h3>SiloAPI traffic</h3>
          <table class="traffic">
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Window</th><th scope="col">Queries</th><th scope="col">Unique clients</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {
                ["1h", "24h", "5d", "30d"].map((w) => (
                  <tr>
                    <td>{w}</td>
                    <td data-q={w}>…</td>
                    <td data-u={w}>…</td>
                  </tr>
                ))
              }
              <tr class="total"><td>total</td><td data-q="total">…</td><td>–</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <h3 class="reach-h">30-day reach</h3>
          <dl class="reach">
            <div><dt>Silo app clients</dt><dd data-r="app">…</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Browse visitors</dt><dd data-r="web">…</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Site visitors</dt><dd data-r="site">…</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="small" data-metrics-note>Counted from our server access logs. We publish only the totals.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // Live numbers. Every value starts as "…" in the HTML and becomes a number or "unavailable";
  // nothing about the catalog is baked into the page.
  // SiloAPI /stats sends its counts as strings ("7030"); accept numbers and numeric strings.
  const fmt = (n: unknown) => {
    const v = typeof n === "string" && n.trim() !== "" ? Number(n) : n;
    return typeof v === "number" && Number.isFinite(v) ? v.toLocaleString("en-US") : "–";
  };
  const json = (u: string) => fetch(u, { credentials: "omit" }).then((r) => (r.ok ? r.json() : Promise.reject(r.status)));
  const tiles = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-live-stats]");
  const api = tiles?.dataset.api;
  const put = (sel: string, v: unknown) => {
    const el = document.querySelector(sel);
    if (el) el.textContent = fmt(v);
  };
  if (api) {
    json(`${api}/stats`)
      .then((s) => {
        put('[data-stat="mods"]', s?.mods);
        put('[data-stat="sources"]', s?.sources);
      })
      .catch(() => {
        put('[data-stat="mods"]', null);
        put('[data-stat="sources"]', null);
      });
    json(`${api}/categories`)
      .then((c) => put('[data-stat="categories"]', Array.isArray(c?.categories) ? c.categories.length : null))
      .catch(() => put('[data-stat="categories"]', null));
  }
  // Release downloads: installer and app-package files only (what a person grabs to install);
  // auto-update polls (latest.json) and .sig checks are machines, not installs.
  const INSTALLER = /\.(exe|msi|dmg|AppImage|deb|rpm)$/i;
  const dl = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-live-downloads]");
  type Rel = { tag_name: string; html_url: string; draft: boolean; prerelease: boolean; assets: { name: string; download_count: number }[] };
  if (dl?.dataset.repoApi) {
    fetch(dl.dataset.repoApi, { credentials: "omit", headers: { Accept: "application/vnd.github+json" } })
      .then((r) => (r.ok ? (r.json() as Promise<Rel[]>) : Promise.reject(r.status)))
      .then((list) => {
        const rels = list
          .filter((r) => !r.draft && !r.prerelease)
          .map((r) => ({
            tag: r.tag_name,
            url: r.html_url,
            installs: r.assets.reduce((n, a) => n + (INSTALLER.test(a.name) ? a.download_count : 0), 0),
            all: r.assets.reduce((n, a) => n + a.download_count, 0),
          }));
        const total = rels.reduce((n, r) => n + r.installs, 0);
        const max = Math.max(1, ...rels.map((r) => r.installs));
        put("[data-dl-total]", total);
        const sub = dl.querySelector("[data-dl-releases]");
        if (sub) sub.textContent = `, ${rels.length} releases`;
        const body = dl.querySelector("[data-dl-rows]");
        const svgNs = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
        for (const r of rels) {
          const tr = document.createElement("tr");
          const tagCell = document.createElement("td");
          const a = document.createElement("a");
          a.href = r.url.startsWith("https://github.com/HLLMR/silo/") ? r.url : "https://github.com/HLLMR/silo/releases";
          a.textContent = r.tag;
          tagCell.append(a);
          const n = document.createElement("td");
          n.textContent = fmt(r.installs);
          const barCell = document.createElement("td");
          barCell.className = "bar-col";
          barCell.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "true");
          const svg = document.createElementNS(svgNs, "svg");
          svg.setAttribute("viewBox", "0 0 100 8");
          svg.setAttribute("preserveAspectRatio", "none");
          const rect = document.createElementNS(svgNs, "rect");
          rect.setAttribute("width", String(Math.max(2, Math.round((r.installs / max) * 100))));
          rect.setAttribute("height", "8");
          rect.setAttribute("rx", "2");
          svg.append(rect);
          barCell.append(svg);
          tr.append(tagCell, n, barCell);
          body?.append(tr);
        }
        const note = dl.querySelector("[data-dl-note]");
        if (note) note.textContent += ` GitHub served ${fmt(rels.reduce((n, r) => n + r.all, 0))} files in total across these releases; the rest are auto-update checks and signature files, not installs.`;
      })
      .catch(() => {
        put("[data-dl-total]", null);
        const note = dl.querySelector("[data-dl-note]");
        if (note) note.textContent = "Release numbers are unavailable right now. See the Releases page on GitHub.";
      });
  }

  const u30 = (o: { uniques?: Record<string, number> } | undefined) => o?.uniques?.["30d"];
  json("/metrics.json")
    .then((m) => {
      const q = m?.api?.queries ?? {};
      const u = m?.api?.uniques ?? {};
      for (const w of ["1h", "24h", "5d", "30d"]) {
        put(`[data-q="${w}"]`, q[w]);
        put(`[data-u="${w}"]`, u[w]);
      }
      put('[data-q="total"]', q.total);
      put('[data-r="app"]', u30(m?.api?.app));
      put('[data-r="web"]', u30(m?.api?.web));
      put('[data-r="site"]', u30(m?.site));
      const note = document.querySelector("[data-metrics-note]");
      if (note && m?.generatedAt) note.textContent += ` Updated ${new Date(m.generatedAt).toLocaleString()}.`;
    })
    .catch(() => {
      for (const el of document.querySelectorAll("[data-live-metrics] td, [data-live-metrics] dd")) {
        if (el.textContent === "…") el.textContent = "–";
      }
      const note = document.querySelector("[data-metrics-note]");
      if (note) note.textContent = "The traffic feed is unavailable right now.";
    });
</script>

<style>
  section {
    padding: 64px 0;
  }
  .narrow {
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .kicker {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--earth-text);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    max-width: 18em;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  p {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  a {
    color: var(--primary-text);
  }
  .btn-primary {
    color: var(--on-primary);
  }
  .btn-ghost {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 20px 0 0;
  }
  .sub {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .small {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 28px 0 36px;
  }
  .tiles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .tiles div {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 18px 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column-reverse;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .tiles dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .tiles dt {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .why {
    background: var(--sunken);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 28px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .cols p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .legend-h {
    margin-top: 36px;
  }
  .legend {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .legend li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px 12px;
  }
  .badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  }
  .badge.ok {
    color: var(--success);
    border-color: var(--success);
  }
  .badge.warn {
    color: var(--warn);
    border-color: var(--warn);
  }
  .badge.none {
    color: var(--muted);
    border-style: dashed;
  }
  .endpoints {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    margin: 12px 0;
    background: var(--sunken);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  code {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .numbers {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .grid2 {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .panel {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: 20px 22px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .big {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin: 4px 0 12px;
  }
  .big span {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.93rem;
  }
  th,
  table :global(td) {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 6px 8px 6px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  th {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  table :global(.bar-col) {
    width: 45%;
  }
  .bars :global(svg) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 8px;
  }
  .bars :global(rect) {
    fill: var(--primary);
  }
  .traffic .total :global(td) {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .reach-h {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  .reach {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(120px, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .reach div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column-reverse;
  }
  .reach dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
  }
  .reach dt {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  .bars :global(a) {
    color: var(--primary-text);
  }
</style>
